{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1195206-homebrew-families-hungers-and-other-family-tree-branches","id":1195206,"title":"Homebrew Families, Hungers and other Family Tree Branches","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-14T03:41:22-07:00","id":1195206,"title":"Homebrew Families, Hungers and other Family Tree Branches","content":"So, I had a random derpy thought. The Families are major Nightmares, things that everyone fears to one degree or another. Are there other concepts that haven't been explored as Families, yet?<br /> Same with Hungers.<br /> Being upfront, I don't really have much of an Idea how one could pull off another family or hunger, but seeing how creative this fanbase is, and how similar we occasionally think to the developers as indicated by the homebrew systems for Horrors<br /> <br /> I thought Death, as the concept of finality and an end to things, has some potential. Not necessarily the &quot;You Die!&quot; route, but more the Brush of Death that makes people realize, and dread, the fact that their life is inevitably coming to an end. Of course, this could extend a bit more - the end of childhood marked by your children moving out, the end of employment marked by you being fired, the end of personal freedom due to responsibilities. The Nightmares of Loss, in a way.<br /> There is, of course, some overlap, especially with Anakim, Makara and Tassilii, but those are bound to happen with Beast families anyway to a degree.<br /> <br /> I'd also be interested in non-human Nightmares. For example, the Insatiables claim to be Nightmares from before humanity, of Earth and Ice and Fire.<br /> So why shouldn't there be Uratha-, Awakened-, Kindred-, Changeling-specific Family Branches?<br /> Of course, this would require that a) those groups share common fears and b) another Family doesn't already deal with it. Maybe instead, these would be distant branches, kind-of similar to Beasts, but still somehow changed? Not a fan of a z-splat for Beast, so not gonna propose that idea.<br /> Still, I dunno why, but I just feel like &quot;Nightmares of the Sun&quot; would make for a fine Kindred Antagonist, and there certainly are very Kindred-like Fears to explore (Fire, the Sun, being Dead, losing grasp of their humanity, losing Control to the Beast, becoming a witless puppet). &quot;Nightmares of Silver&quot; could be the opposite of the mercurial shapeshifting Uratha, unchanging and mocking the Hunt. Nightmares of the Lie could play with concepts of Hubris and Pride, misguided power (you are not powerless to do something, but you still mess up) etc.<br /> <br /> Those are just some things from the top of my head, no checking or reflecting involved. Still, I wanna hear your thoughts: Is there room for more Families? Which ones could you think of?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T11:03:31-07:00","id":1195379,"title":"","content":"I think there was a thread that made mention of a Family representing Fear of Conflict...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17107-mangaholic13","name":"Mangaholic13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T17:12:16-07:00","id":1195532,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Well, I was planning on stockpiling this for a homebrew thread but I\u2019m enough of a fussy perfectionist I don\u2019t think I\u2019ll ever be able to post it any time soon. Not too long after I picked up the Beast core a year ago (and loved it even with the criticisms I have-- most of which are assuaged by the PG) I started working on what I felt like was a mythic archetype missing from the book.<br /> <br /> I wanted to make a Family of tricksters and the concept I decided to work from was the Nightmare of Betrayal. I think this is a pretty core fear to the human existence, given how humans are highly social creatures and close emotional connections are vital to psychological health. It might be a bit more cerebral than a lot of the more primal fears expressed by other Beasts (barring perhaps the Inguma) but I think it could have a niche.<br /> <br /> Speaking of the Inguma, they\u2019re why this little project was on hold for so long. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I was worried they\u2019d cross over with my concept once I heard of them. I\u2019m tentatively calling them the Iktomi after the spider trickster from Lakota folklore, though I also considered Gumiho. And they did, a bit, I had to throw out the Atavism I had designed around shapeshifting, but I think after some very minor retooling they might stand on their own?<br /> <br /> My justification for this is that Inguma represent more fears of...well, the outsider. The one who doesn\u2019t quite fit in once you give them a bit of scrutiny, and the fact they\u2019re close to being \u201cright\u201d just makes things more unnerving. The Iktomi ooze their way in and out of society and, quite often, are everyone\u2019s best friend. They\u2019re smarmy con artists or thieves who you don\u2019t realize have stolen from you until you\u2019re robbed blind-- at least, when they\u2019re at their best. It\u2019s the Other versus That Person You Thought You Knew.<br /> <br /> Or, well, the above is more an example of a Collector, but you get the point. They like getting up close and personal to their prey.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m still in the process of working out the Birthrights but I have what I think is a solid concept for one, lovingly poached from Werewolf the Apocalypse. Once a chapter they can say any true statement to a person and have it be interpreted as a lie, so long as that lie does not violate inherent laws of the universe, and the target only believes it is a lie for the remainder of the chapter. As I mentioned I had to toss a few Atavisms (I had one too close to Enemy Within and another too close to Doppelganger) but I\u2019m...getting to a working prototype.<br /> <br /> My design theme for the Atavisms was to emphasize their role as social predators (and a secondary one that just makes them very good at getting away from things fast, because being able to run is a good trait for a trickster, I would say.) Makara, Ugallu, and Anakim all have some abilities that enhance their social prowess but I don\u2019t feel like this is a primary theme for any, so I hope that\u2019s not stepping on any proverbial toes here.<br /> <br /> I have a fancily-formatted version of all this I\u2019m still in the process of writing, but again, inveterate perfectionist who hasn\u2019t learned that perfect is the enemy of done, so hopefully I can make myself finally break down and finish it someday. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raziel MacPhereson, he/they | <a href=\"http://twitter.com/beastsoulfury\" target=\"_blank\">Twitter</a> | <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Raziel%20MacPhereson\" target=\"_blank\">STV Content</a> | <a href=\"https://huntunderironskies.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Tumblr</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23812-cherubic","name":"Cherubic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23812_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}